From 50e2848f376529222adc6307967cac999f46d457 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:28:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/20] tu: Add VK_EXT_mesh_shader for A8XX

Implement VK_EXT_mesh_shader on A8XX using the hardware mesh path: the
CP_DRAW_MESH-style 0x7a packet that the SQE forwards to the AQE firmware.
The AQE launches task and mesh workgroups in batches and then draws the
generated primitives. Mesh shaders are lowered to compute programs that
write vertex, index and per-primitive records into a driver scratch buffer
using the layout the firmware expects. A stub vertex shader pulls those
records for the graphics stage.

Supported:
 - task shaders with payloads up to 16 KiB;
 - direct, indirect and indirect-count draws;
 - per-primitive outputs, including aggregate types;
 - cull primitives;
 - point lists via the hardware point-list record;
 - multiview, with the per-view loop in the shader;
 - mesh and task pipeline statistics queries;
 - pipeline libraries.

Shapes the native path does not handle yet fall back to a compute
emulation path: compute + barrier + an indexed draw through a pass-through
vertex shader.

Mesh render passes always use sysmem rendering, as the proprietary driver
does.

The feature is behind TU_EXPERIMENTAL=mesh_shader (emulation only), plus
mesh_native for the hardware path. This adds the TU_EXPERIMENTAL
environment variable.

VK-CTS on Adreno 840 (KGSL), TU_EXPERIMENTAL=mesh_shader,mesh_native:
  dEQP-VK.mesh_shader.ext.*                   26391 pass, 0 fail, 547 not supported
  dEQP-VK.multiview.*                           811 pass, 0 fail,  27 not supported
Emulation only (TU_EXPERIMENTAL=mesh_shader):
  dEQP-VK.mesh_shader.ext.*                    1617 pass, 8 fail, 25313 not supported
